{'symbol': 'CHD', 'date': '2019-10-31 22:30:00', 'title': 'ROBERT D. LEBLANC ANNOUNCES RETIREMENT FROM THE BOARD OF CHURCH & DWIGHT CO., INC', 'text': 'ON OCTOBER 30, 2019, ROBERT D. LEBLANC NOTIFIED THE BOARD OF DIRECTORS OF CHURCH & DWIGHT CO., INC. THAT HE INTENDS TO RETIRE FROM THE BOARD AND WILL, THEREFORE, NOT STAND FOR REELECTION AS A MEMBER OF THE BOARD AT THE COMPANY’S ANNUAL MEETING OF STOCKHOLDERS TO BE HELD ON APRIL 30, 2020. MR. LEBLANC WILL CONTINUE TO SERVE ON THE BOARD AND AS LEAD DIRECTOR AND AS A MEMBER OF THE AUDIT COMMITTEE AND THE EXECUTIVE COMMITTEE UNTIL THE END OF HIS TERM, WHICH WILL EXPIRE AT THE END OF THE 2020 ANNUAL MEETING OR WHEN HIS SUCCESSOR HAS BEEN ELECTED AND QUALIFIED. THE COMPANY GRATEFULLY ACKNOWLEDGES MR. LEBLANC’S MORE THAN TWO DECADES OF DEDICATED SERVICE ON ITS BOARD. MR. LEBLANC’S DECISION NOT TO SEEK REELECTION WAS NOT THE RESULT OF ANY DISAGREEMENT WITH THE COMPANY.'}{'symbol': 'CHD', 'date': '2019-10-31 09:30:00', 'title': 'CHURCH & DWIGHT REPORTS Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE $0.62', 'text': 'CHURCH & DWIGHT REPORTS Q3 RESULTS.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE $0.62.Q3 SALES $1.089 BILLION VERSUS REFINITIV IBES ESTIMATE OF $1.1 BILLION.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $0.61 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.SEES Q4 SALES UP ABOUT 6 PERCENT.FY ORGANIC SALES GROWTH MAINTAINED +4%.SEES FY 2019 SALES GROWTH UP 5%.FY FORECAST FOR CASH FROM OPERATIONS RAISED TO APPROXIMATELY $815 MILLION.SEES FY ADJUSTED EPS MAINTAINED AT $2.47.CHURCH & DWIGHT CO -Q3 ORGANIC SALES GREW 3.6% DRIVEN BY POSITIVE PRODUCT MIX AND PRICING OF 4.3% PARTIALLY OFFSET BY A VOLUME DECLINE OF 0.7%.QTRLY ADJUSTED. EARNINGS PER SHARE $0.66.INTEND TO ACCELERATE $4 MILLION OF INVESTMENTS IN OUR LONG-TERM ASIA PACIFIC RELATIONSHIPS IN Q4.FY2019 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $2.49, REVENUE VIEW $4.39 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.INTEND TO MAKE INCREMENTAL INVESTMENTS IN Q4 AS A RESULT OF OUR STRONG RESULTS AND TARIFF RELIEF.Q4 REVENUE VIEW $1.16 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.'}{'symbol': 'CHD', 